WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:05.180
Hey youtubers it’s charlie and this week
Arrow came back from Olympics hiatus and wasted

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:07.120
no time picking up the pace.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:11.990
We got more River Song, Robert Knepper playing
a character from the comic books, two major

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:15.540
plot lines set up a long time ago were paid
off and we got some of the best Felicity scenes

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:16.540
of the season.

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:19.140
In all fairness this really was her episode.

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:20.690
Also quick Flash Spin off shoutout.

00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:22.080
They’ll be filming the pilot starting next
week.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.430
So I’m going to wait to do a video till
then.

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:26.200
Hopefully there will be lots of great behind
the scenes pictures.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.220
If you’re finding me for the first time
be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:31.470
I am still doing my weekly Arrow Q&amp;A tomorrow
though.

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:35.039
Now since there were so many good things in
the episode let’s do top 5 moments, then

00:00:35.039 --> 00:00:38.399
I’ll do a breakdown of the comic book references
and my review.

00:00:38.399 --> 00:00:40.629
Careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
the episode.

00:00:40.629 --> 00:00:44.140
But Number 5 - Oliver and Sarah go everywhere
together now.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:47.559
The funniest part of this is that his own
daughter is standing right in front of him

00:00:47.559 --> 00:00:50.319
and he still doesn’t know who they are.

00:00:50.319 --> 00:00:53.649
I loved that Oliver even referred to himself
in third person.

00:00:53.649 --> 00:00:57.430
This is going to keep happening this season
and hopefully into season 3 if the Birds of

00:00:57.430 --> 00:00:59.329
Prey development continues like the showrunners
are planning.

00:00:59.329 --> 00:01:01.639
Number 4 - Felicity Training Session.

00:01:01.639 --> 00:01:03.359
What are you wearing.

00:01:03.359 --> 00:01:06.970
Emilly Bett Rickards actually said that she’s
not jealous of Oliver and Sara in a traditional

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:10.570
way, but she is upset at the thought of losing
the closeness that they have.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:13.720
It’s pretty clear that Sara saw through
it all and since they’re destined to become

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:17.050
the Birds of Prey I’m really looking forward
to how they deal with it.

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:20.220
I’m sure Felicity will get through it with
plenty of Wushu and punching.

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:23.780
It’s really just fun to see her see some
action away from her computer console.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:26.810
It would have been a little more fun if she
had been wearing batgirl colors though.

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:31.540
Since it’s kind of implied she’s going
to become the Oracle character.

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:33.730
Number 3 - The Stunts.

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:36.040
Most notably during the climax at the bank.

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:39.790
Oliver sliding down staircases backwards while
shooting arrows.

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:42.930
Felicity taking a bullet mid-air while blowing
up Clock King.

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:47.409
James Bamford is the stunt coordinator so
he’s responsible for the awesome fight scenes.

00:01:47.409 --> 00:01:51.580
You may remember him from Stargate Atlantis
and all the awesome fights Jason Momoa got

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:53.420
to have.

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:55.880
Number 2 - Felicity Vs Sara Science Off.

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:59.890
The blood analysis was just the most fun part
of the Felicity versus Sara story arc.

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:03.800
I felt so bad for her when it seemed like
Sara science’d her into submission.

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:06.920
That look on her face will live in tumblr
infamy forever.

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:09.640
I’ll say that felicity did get the last
laugh.

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:14.099
She saved Sara, took a bullet from her and
was still worried that she killed Clock King.

00:02:14.099 --> 00:02:18.450
It’s like the writers want her to be a badass
without compromising her morals or getting

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:19.450
vicious like Sara.

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:23.599
and my Number 1 moment - Drunk Naked Felicity
Speechifying.

00:02:23.599 --> 00:02:26.319
Everyone run for cover because this totally
made tumblr explode.

00:02:26.319 --> 00:02:30.409
It’s amazing at how the show damages their
relationship and then puts it back together

00:02:30.409 --> 00:02:31.409
in an instant.

00:02:31.409 --> 00:02:33.840
I can’t wait to see the outtake reel from
this scene.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:35.760
Just the part where she fumbles over her words.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:40.510
I would like to thank Diggle and I would like
to thank oxycotin for this wonderful performance.

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:42.799
Somebody needs to give Felicity a drunk Oscar.

00:02:42.799 --> 00:02:47.390
It’s like the normal Oscars, but only for
performances given while you're drunk.

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:50.139
one last bonus best moment - Slade reveals
himself publicly.

00:02:50.139 --> 00:02:54.360
He’s not hiding or appearing to Green Arrow
first, he went to Moira.

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:56.420
Probably to get involved with her run for
Mayor.

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:59.610
He’s really just letting Oliver know that
he can kill them all at any moment.

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:02.881
The teaser for the next episode featured scenes
that pick up directly where this last scene

00:03:02.881 --> 00:03:03.881
left off.

00:03:03.881 --> 00:03:08.269
So we won’t have to wait long to see what
the quote unquote Promise between them is.

00:03:08.269 --> 00:03:10.749
So let me know what your favorite moment was.

00:03:10.749 --> 00:03:12.920
I know, we’re all thinking the same thing.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:14.439
You’ll always be my girl.

00:03:14.439 --> 00:03:16.349
It’s just too much.

00:03:16.349 --> 00:03:20.450
Here are all the references I saw, there were
a few really important ones.

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:22.029
Starting with Kord Industries.

00:03:22.029 --> 00:03:24.650
This was where William Tockman, the Clock
King worked.

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:28.540
They’ve mentioned Kord Industries in so
many different episodes including Grant Gustin’s

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:32.370
Flash episodes, that I’m wondering if they’re
laying the groundwork for Ted Kord to guest

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:34.040
star on the show in Season 3.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:36.349
And then eventually the Blue Beetle.

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:38.090
Then there was Sara’s Bar, Oblivion.

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:42.319
This is the home base of Shadowpact and it
exists in a pocket dimension that overlaps

00:03:42.319 --> 00:03:43.629
with several other universes.

00:03:43.629 --> 00:03:48.549
So it’s like a nexus of the multiverse where
you can grab a drink and hire a magic user.

00:03:48.549 --> 00:03:52.840
Then there was Alex Kingston talking about
being a history professor in Central City

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:54.599
and having another man.

00:03:54.599 --> 00:03:59.139
The easy one is the professor River Song reference,
meaning that other man could be The Doctor

00:03:59.139 --> 00:04:02.000
and Central City is where the Flash show will
take place.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:05.769
So her character could also be a backdoor
to bring Arrow people onto that show.

00:04:05.769 --> 00:04:11.189
Overall I gave the episode an A minus for
excellent use of Emily Bett Rickards and because

00:04:11.189 --> 00:04:14.120
it paid off the Sin storyline and Slade.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:17.380
They’ve been teasing a Villains arc on the
show that’s going to start soon and cross

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:18.850
four or five episodes.

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:23.730
For a show that has to fill an hour of time
every week and has 23 episodes Arrow does

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:28.010
such an amazing job of weaving in new characters
and side stories that keep it feeling fresh

00:04:28.010 --> 00:04:29.010
every week.

00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:32.040
To be fair to other shows like Supernatural,
it’s been around for 9 years.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:34.080
So I don’t expect the same things from it.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:37.760
The only thing that felt out of place in this
episode was Thea, it felt like if you had

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:40.750
cut all her lines nothing about the story
would have changed.

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:44.230
And the call she made to Oliver at the end
felt like it was either Slade hacking her

00:04:44.230 --> 00:04:48.480
phone or something the writers created purely
as a reason to get him into the house while

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:49.480
Slade was there.

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:50.480
Let me know what you thought of the episode.

